  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="16ab6c7a-e03f-5d81-9de5-227f720f5536" activityNameId="6118210c-d397-5a9f-aa8c-da5cf6de44ef" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Photovoltaic cell, ribbon-Si, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Photovoltaic cell, ribbon-Si, at plant
Production of photovoltaic cells (156*156 mm2). Some inputs and emissions aggregated to protect sensitive data. with an efficiency of 13.7%. Wafer thickness 250um.;
Synonyms: polycrystalline, multi-crystalline, silicon; 
UUID: 2f266521-7e7c-32a4-aeb7-d139afdcd6b9
Cleaning, damage etching, texture etching, covering of backside, phosphor dotation, phosphor glass etching, printing of contacts, cleaning and quality testing.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average production technology of photovoltaic cells from wafers.
Time period: Data investigated in 2004 and recalculated for the cell size in 2005.
Production volume: Total worldwide production 1727MW in 2000.
Sampling: Data collected from 5 specific processes and companies (4 multi-Si + 1 single-Si processing company). 
Extrapolations: Data 2005 calculated from data 2004 by multiplying amounts of materials by solar cell area factor of 156*156/(125*125) = 1.56; energy scaled linearly with cell side length.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2f266521-7e7c-32a4-aeb7-d139afdcd6b9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
